# UX workflow: canonical Pattern and matrix Track selection lifecycle.
# Purpose: proves that the same mechanical grammar used by Macro remains true
# while Pattern selection stays in the editor and Project-wide Track selection
# belongs to explicit matrix headers.
# Step selection is covered by structure/step-selection.ux.
# Expect: capture_changed:pattern_selected=pattern_selection_placing
# Expect: capture_changed:pattern_selection_placing=pattern_selection_pasted
# Expect: capture_changed:track_selected=track_selection_placing
# Expect: capture_changed:track_selection_placing=track_selection_pasted

0 scenario sequencer
80 capture screen pattern_ready

# Stationary NAV hold enters Pattern selection; Copy previews the next page.
180 button NAV down
1260 tick
1340 button NAV up
1520 tap NAV 60
1740 capture screen pattern_selected
1840 tap BOTTOM_RIGHT 60
2060 capture screen pattern_selection_placing
2160 encoder NAV 0.01
2360 capture screen pattern_selection_destination
2460 button BOTTOM_RIGHT down
3540 tick
3620 button BOTTOM_RIGHT up
3860 capture screen pattern_selection_pasted

# Back clears the placement first, then exits the armed selection.
3960 tap LEFT_TOP 60
4180 capture screen pattern_selection_cleared
4280 tap LEFT_TOP 60
4500 capture screen pattern_selection_exited

# Back returns to the exact matrix Clip; one reverse turn reaches its Track
# header. Repeat the same lifecycle there with a Project-wide payload.
4600 tap LEFT_TOP 60
4820 capture screen launcher_returned
4920 encoder NAV -0.01
5120 capture screen track_header_ready
5220 button NAV down
6300 tick
6380 button NAV up
6560 tap NAV 60
6780 capture screen track_selected
6880 tap BOTTOM_RIGHT 60
7100 capture screen track_selection_placing
7200 encoder NAV 0.01
7400 capture screen track_selection_destination
7500 button BOTTOM_RIGHT down
8580 tick
8660 button BOTTOM_RIGHT up
8980 capture screen track_selection_pasted
9080 tap LEFT_TOP 60
9300 capture screen track_selection_cleared
9400 tap LEFT_TOP 60
9620 capture screen track_selection_exited
